STATEMENT OF CHANGES (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

This repository is a derivative work of the upstream repository above. The upstream commit is kept in the
git history unmodified; all later commits are changes made by Lee Marshall, with the new code and text
generated by Claude (Anthropic) under his direction. The changes relative to upstream commit d189594 are:

  1. Added Lean modules: ThreeRiseCheck, MCycleSteps3, MCycleChain3, ThreeRiseSplit, MCycleThreeRise105,
     MCycleThreeRiseN203, MCycleThreeRiseN325_*, MCycleGrid3_*, TwoRiseCheck2, TwoRiseCheck3, WalkSplit,
     TwoRise2_*, MCycleTwoRise102, MCycleTwoRise103, MCycleGrid102 ... MCycleGrid111, MCycle102 ... MCycle111
     (with their *Def, *Shapes, *Walk*, *Certs*, *Data modules), LogTwoThreeBounds80, MCycleChain3D, BenchKernel.
     These prove, from the same two hypotheses as upstream, that every nontrivial positive Collatz cycle has at
     least 112 local minima (Collatz.no_111_cycle_2_71), extending upstream's bound of 102.
  2. Modified: Collatz.lean (added imports of MCycle102, MCycle103, MCycle111); scripts/Statement.lean (added
     statements main_statement_102 ... main_statement_111 and updated the header comment);
     .github/workflows/lean.yml (manual trigger only, longer timeout); README.md (rewritten).
  3. Added scripts and data: scripts/build_serial.py; research/scripts/mcycle103_split, mcycle105,
     mcycle107, mcycle109 and research/scripts/lean127 (generators of the new Lean modules); AXIOM_AUDIT.txt; METHOD.md; computed/
     (Python programs and certificate summaries for the computed extension to m <= 127).
